STAFF REPORT - SUMMATION

Summit Park

Preliminary Plat Process

CASE NUMBER:
UDC-15-00420

SUBDIVISION CODE: SMTP-P

PREPARED BY:
Brandon Cammarata

MEETING DATES:
August 3, 2015 – Planning Commission
August 10, 2015 – City Council

REQUIRED DOCUMENTS SUBMISSION: The following required documents have been submitted and
reviewed by staff.

●
Complete Application
●
Preliminary Plat Map
●
Drainage Worksheet
●
Transportation Worksheet
●
Environmental Impact Assessment

PLANNING COMMISSION UPDATE (8/4/15): At its’ regular meeting on August 3, 2015, the motion
to approve the preliminary plat with staff recommendation #1 failed by a vote of 2-4.  Concerns identified
by Planning Commission where traffic and concerns with the wording of the notification letter.  The
notification letter is not required with a preliminary plat.  The Planning Commission felt the wording of
“15 unit multi-family complex” did not adequately translate to the concept proposed of 60 units in 15
buildings.

From a traffic standpoint that applicant completed the required transportation worksheet which identified
the proposal would be below regulatory thresholds and additional analysis was not warranted.

On August 4, 2015, the agent expressed the desire to continue to take the project to the City Council.

RECOMMENDATION: The Development Department recommends the City Council amend the Planning
Commission recommendation and acknowledge the preliminary plat with staff recommendation #1.

1. Please dedicate a 20’x20’ triangle of additional right-of-way on the corner of Summit & Ridge to
provide additional right-of-way for future signalization and other intersection improvements.
```

