### Page 6 of 10

```text
Preliminary Plat/UDC-15-00420
6
multifamily complex would require a conditional use approval.  Setbacks and coverage for the complex
are described in Lot Type MD1 for the multifamily complex as a whole.  Design standards described in
Article 6 are required as applicable and reviewed via administrative site plan approval.

Lot 16 is identified as a proposed location for a sanitary sewer lift station which is substantially an
underground facility with a box above ground, similar to a CLFP utility box, which would be about 5-feet
tall and 8 feet x 8 feet.  A lot is not required for such a facility and could be accommodated with
easements.  The location should be one that minimizes impacts to the site.  Staff will coordinate with the
BOPU and the applicant regarding approaches to this utility feature prior to final plat submittal.

The existing single family residences on Lots 1 and 2 are allowable in the proposed zone district and
would not require any modifications other than connecting to sanitary sewer when annexed.

SURROUNDING DEVELOPMENT - The application will not create any undue influence on existing or potential
development for adjacent property considering the existing zoning and Comprehensive Plan policies for
that property.

This is an area currently developed with a hodgepodge of rural residential development in the County.
PlanCheyenne supports the transition of this area to urban development taking advantage of nearby
infrastructure and logical provision of services. Typically residential uses are compatible with other
surrounding residential uses. Higher intensity residential uses such as multifamily are supported by direct
access to a major thoroughfare which is available in Summit Drive with access in to the City via Storey
Boulevard and Ridge Road.  Proximity to north Cheyenne Community Park is also considered an asset to
higher density residential development.

With this project the applicant identified they sent mailed notice to 21 surrounding landowners as well as
signed notice on the property.

REVIEWERS w/ COMMENTS:
-
Board of Public Utilities (Linda Gunter) On this Preliminary Plat, if any of the easement are going to
be designated for BOPU’s water and sewer mains. The Utility easement must read BOPU Utility
Easement. Any lot that will used for a Sewer Lift or Water Pump Station the must be 50’ by 50’ in
size.

There is no water or sewer available to serve this development. Owner/developer is responsible for
verifying the remaining available sewer capacity of the existing sewer system in the area to serve this
project. The developer will be required to construct a looped water main to serve this development.
The property Owner/developer shall be required to extend the water and sanitary sewer utilities from
their current location to the farthest point (or points) of the property being developed. These utility
extensions shall be to a point (or points) that are logical for projected future connections to future
development projects, as determined by the BOPU and the property owner/developer.

The BOPU needs to approve all water and sewer main design layout. All water and sanitary sewer
utilities has to be designed and constructed in accordance with the latest City of Cheyenne and Board
of Public Utilities Construction Specifications Standards and Standard Drawings and the latest Rules &
Regulations for Establishing Policies & Design Criteria of the Board of Public Utilities Cheyenne,
Wyoming.
